  "readmeFile": "README.md",
  "releaseNotes": "0.3.0: theming, mobile support and accessibility. Upgrade by bumping the package version; no code changes are required.\n- Themes: configure RazorKitOptions.Themes (a list of Name and DataTheme) to get a theme dropdown in the toolbar; the preview is rendered with data-theme set to the chosen theme. The choice is kept in the URL (?theme=) and remembered in the browser. With no themes configured the preview sets no theme. The old built-in \"charity\" default theme is removed: if your site relied on it, add it to RazorKitOptions.Themes.\n- Mobile: on narrow screens the component list and the Controls panel become slide-out panels (one open at a time) and the preview uses the device width.\n- Accessibility: RazorKit's own interface now uses real buttons, keyboard navigation, visible focus, labelled controls and improved contrast (working towards WCAG 2.2 AA).\n- Edits in the Controls panel now survive viewport and theme changes.\n- \"Open in new window\" opens the current, edited preview in a new tab.\n- A single reset button (\"Reset to story values\", or \"Reset to defaults\" when the story sets no values) replaces the two previous ones.\n- When a preview is refused (for example too many requests), the preview area shows a short readable message.\n- GET previews now count towards the render concurrency limit (MaxConcurrentRenders), and viewport or theme changes with edited values count as renders.\n- RazorKit's page script and styles are now served as package files rather than inline, so a host Content-Security-Policy no longer needs to allow inline script for RazorKit's page (inline styles are still used).\n- RazorKit's HTML pages (explorer, preview and rejection pages) now carry a robots noindex meta tag, so they stay unindexed even if a proxy or CDN strips the X-Robots-Tag header.\n- Fixed: editing a story in the Controls panel (or switching viewport or theme) no longer breaks components whose props are typed as an interface or object.",
